{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553568-murderer","id":1553568,"title":"Murderer","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-08-31T15:22:53-07:00","id":1553568,"title":"Murderer","content":"Really, is something i can't totally understand of the game, killing anything will always result in banality or not? Do changeling kill or not kill at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28667-kaioser8","name":"KaioSer8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-31T17:49:20-07:00","id":1553572,"title":"","content":"If you're not a Wilder, killing some things are a Banality trigger. Killing most mortals or prodigals isn't a Banality trigger for anyone though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-31T21:01:33-07:00","id":1553574,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that any entity that comes from the Dreaming (including Changelings) are a dream. You're not just taking a life, you're damaging (or potentially destroying) a dream... making the world a lesser place and hastening the Winter of Banality where creativity and imagination freeze.<br /> <br /> So yeah, changelings take killing a bit harder than many others due. They can't exist if the stuff they're made off is driven from the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-15T00:15:34-07:00","id":1558864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaioSer8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1553568-murderer#post1553568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, is something i can't totally understand of the game, killing anything will always result in banality or not? Do changeling kill or not kill at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Death is different for Changelings.<br /> <br /> When they die, they don't go to the Shadowlands like humans do. Instead, their faerie soul immediately wanders off to find a new human to merge with. This reincarnation cycle typically suppresses the memories of their previous lives, but these memories can resurface again if they venture deep enough into The Dreaming.<br /> <br /> <br /> The exception to this is if the Changeling is slain by Cold Iron, as doing so will result in the destruction of their faerie soul and end their reincarnation. <b>Most</b> Changelings can not even handle the touch of Cold Iron without accruing Banality, except for members of House Balor. Simply touching Cold Iron won't harm them, but wounds inflicted by it are still deadly.<br /> <br /> Of course, this gives House Balor an edge in combat, as they are free to wield Cold Iron weapons against their enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}